==English==
[[Image:Nozyczki4.jpg|thumb|right|upright=1|an assortment of scissors]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|cizars|cizers||both obsolete}}
* {{alter|en|scissars||archaic}}
* {{alter|en|sissors||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|sisours}} (attested since 1350–1400), from {{der|en|fro|[[cisoir]]s}}, from {{der|en|LL.|cīsōria}}, plural of {{m|la|cīsōrium||cutting tool}}; from {{der|en|la|-}} word root {{m|la||-cīsus}} (compare {{m|en|excise}}) or {{m|la|caesus}}, past participle of {{m|la|caedō||to cut}}. Partially displaced native {{ncog|ang|sċēara||scissors, shears}}, whence {{m|en|shears}}. {{doublet|en|chisel}}.

The current spelling, from the 16th century, is due to association with {{der|en|ML.|scissor||tailor}}, from {{der|en|la|-}} carrying the meaning “carver, cutter”, from {{m|la|scindō|t=to split}}. {{rfv-etym|en}}

