===Noun===
{{en-noun|p|attr=scissor}}
{{wikipedia|Scissors}}
{{wikipedia|Scissors (aeronautics)}}

# {{lb|en|countable|usually|construed as plural}} A [[tool]] used for [[cut]]ting thin material, consisting of two crossing blades attached at a [[pivot]] point in such a way that the blades slide across each other when the handles are closed.
#: {{ux|en|Those '''scissors''' are sharp.|q=indicating singular or plural scissors}}
#: {{ux|en|That '''scissors''' is sharp.|q=less commonly to indicate singular scissors}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Scissors''' are used to cut the flowers.}}
#: {{ux|en|Use '''scissors''' to cut them if you don't have proper shears.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Around the Garden|work=New York Times|date=Jun 22, 1947|passage=Roses will last longer if a knife rather than a '''scissors''' is used to cut the blooms.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|aviation|military|with '''''the'''''}} A type of [[defensive]] [[maneuver]] in [[dogfight]]ing, involving [[repeatedly]] [[turn]]ing one's [[aircraft]] [[towards]] that of the [[attacker]] in order to [[force]] them to [[overshoot]].
# {{lb|en|countable|aviation|military}} An instance of the above dogfighting maneuver.
# {{lb|en|countable|rugby}} An [[attack]]ing [[move]] [[conduct]]ed by [[two]] [[player]]s; the player without the [[ball]] [[run]]s from one [[side]] of the [[ball carrier]], [[behind]] the ball [[carrier]], and [[receive]]s a [[pass]] from the ball carrier on the other side.
#: {{ux|en|They executed a perfect '''scissors'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|skating}} A method of skating with one foot significantly in front of the other.
# {{lb|en|countable|gymnastics}} An exercise in which the legs are switched back and forth, suggesting the motion of scissors.
# {{lb|en|countable|wrestling}} A [[scissors hold]].
# {{lb|en|[[rock paper scissors]]}} A [[hand]] with the [[index finger|index]] and [[middle finger|middle]] fingers open (a [[handshape]] resembling scissors), that beats [[paper]] and loses to [[rock]]. It beats [[lizard]] and loses to [[Spock]] in [[rock-paper-scissors-lizard-Spock]].

====Usage notes====
* "A pair of scissors" is preferred to "a scissors" by about a four-to-one margin in the US ([[COCA]]).
* "The scissors" is preferred to "the scissor" by about a thirty-to-one margin in the US ([[COCA]]).

